# Title: ETW Trace Evasion Activity
# ID: a238b5d0-ce2d-4414-a676-7a531b3d13d6
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: @neu5ron, Florian Roth (Nextron Systems), Jonhnathan Ribeiro, oscd.community
# Date: 2019-03-22
# Tags: attack.stealth, attack.defense-impairment, attack.t1070, attack.t1685, car.2016-04-002
# Description: Detects command line activity that tries to clear or disable any ETW trace log which could be a sign of logging evasion.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (((process_exec="*cl*" AND process_exec="*/Trace*")) OR ((process_exec="*clear-log*" AND process_exec="*/Trace*")) OR ((process_exec="*sl*" AND process_exec="*/e:false*")) OR ((process_exec="*set-log*" AND process_exec="*/e:false*")) OR ((process_exec="*logman*" AND process_exec="*update*" AND process_exec="*trace*" AND process_exec="*--p*" AND process_exec="*-ets*")) OR (process_exec="*Remove-EtwTraceProvider*") OR ((process_exec="*Set-EtwTraceProvider*" AND process_exec="*0x11*")))
